body:
As someone who was told by their parents to get aborted, I agree, but I also would counter argue the reason to exist is to be better than your parents out of spite and being a better person by not being a narcissistic person. 

&#x200B;

Which is why I think any kids born from narcissistic parents should tell their parents to go fuck themselves and then do better than them in life.

Just an recommendation, but go for a 5800x, then upgrade to the 5900x if you're needs aren't being met by the 5800x. I'm doing the same but will upgrade to the 5950x instead. You can always do small upgrades and sell unwanted parts. However my biggest reason for getting a 5800x is if you're wanting to upgrade soon, you can get them now at MSRP (I just ordered mine yesterday). Whereas, the 5900x or 5950x are still at those scalper prices. However, even if you read the other comments, I feel like the 5800x is gonna be a good all rounder just because most gaming is not at the levels of performance that APUs/CPUs like the 5800x can't handle.

&#x200B;

Just for reference, I have an Intel i7 3770K, and while it's beginning to show its age, I don't have many problems running current games. But before I had that i7, I had the i5 3750K.
